HST Office: the transitions gallery of the Slides ribbon, and an undoable command that applies a transition.

- .uno:HstApplyTransition?Transition:string=<set id> (SID_HST_APPLY_TRANSITION) applies the first variant
  of a transition set of the Slide Transition deck (transitions.xml set ids, "None" removes it) to the
  selected slides (the current slide without a slide pane) as one undo action, keeping duration, sound
  and advance. Its state is the set id of the selected slides (empty when they differ), disabled for
  read-only documents and views without slides. Normal view and slide sorter handle it.
- The toolbox item of .uno:HstApplyTransition in Slides gets HstTransitionGalleryControl: one row of
  transition thumbnails (sd/cmd/transition-*.png, the deck's icons) labelled with the set names; click
  or Enter applies, the current transition is selected and paged into view; ◂ ▸ page, ▾ opens the
  Slide Transition deck. Placing the item in the ribbon is the Slides content patch's job.
- Rollback: org.openoffice.Office.HSTRibbon/SlidesEffectGalleries off hides the item; the command
  stays.

- sd/inc/app.hrc, sd/sdi/{sdraw,drviewsh,SlideSorterController}.sdi, sd/source/ui/view/drviews{2,7}.cxx,
  sd/source/ui/slidesorter/shell/SlideSorterViewShell.cxx, sd/Library_sd.mk, sd/UIConfig_simpress.mk,
  sd/util/sd.component, Controller.xcu, DrawImpressCommands.xcu.
- New: sd/source/ui/inc/HstTransitionApply.hxx, sd/source/ui/animations/HstTransitionApply.cxx,
  sd/source/ui/controller/HstTransitionGallery.cxx, sd/uiconfig/simpress/ui/hsttransitiongallery.ui.

